# Plan before building

Before writing or installing any code for a UI request, produce a short
explicit checklist in your response (not hidden reasoning) listing the
distinct UI pieces involved. This is intentionally visible to the user so
the process is auditable.

Example, for "build a dashboard":

```
Plan:
- [ ] Sidebar navigation
- [ ] Top bar / user menu
- [ ] Stat cards (x3)
- [ ] Data table
- [ ] Empty/loading states
```

Rules for the plan:

- Break requests into the smallest reasonable named UI pieces (sidebar,
  navbar, cards, table, form, modal, etc.), not "the page" as one item.
- Order matters: layout-defining pieces (sidebar, navbar, page shell)
  before content pieces (cards, tables) before polish (empty states,
  loading states).
- If the request is a single small component ("add a button"), a
  one-line plan is fine — don't pad it.
- After the plan, proceed piece by piece through `02-registry-search.mdc`
  for each item before writing final code.
